        "answer": "They are different lifecycle stages. The Review tab (`review` in `REQ_TABS`) runs after execution. `review_panel` shows `REPORT.md` (the executor's final report, written at the end of the run) with per-repo branch/merge state and trace lint. Plan approval (`plan` tab) happens before execution. `REPORT.md` is required by the executor prompt and bound on completion; it is not produced by the plan-approval step. The Review tab's \"Trazabilidad\" section reads `tr.lint`, not a planner report.",
