      {
        "id": "Q4",
        "answer": "The reusable producer is `bt_planner/cli.py` `run(\"report\", ...)`. It builds a presentation-independent dict: `quality.analyze(plan)` (critical path and distributions), plus `traceability.coverage_report`, `interfaces.report`, and `quality.verification_report` for schema ≥1.2.0. The `emit` callback is the only presentation hook. Validation output is `contract.Report` (`ok`, `errors`, `warnings`). The adapter boundary is `bt_plan_adapter.py`, the only module importing `bt_planner` (line 14). `run_cli` forwards actions to `planner_cli.run` and attaches compatibility data, and `plan_compatibility_report` in `bt_scheduler_adapter.py` supplies compatibility data. A future UI would consume these through `bt_plan_adapter`. This is inferred from the existing wiring; I did not implement anything.",
